==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|steinn||stone}}, from {{inh|is|gmq-pro|ᛊᛏᚨᛁᚾᚨᛉ}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*stainaz||stone}}. Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|stone}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{m|en|Stein}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|steen}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|sten}}, {{etyl|nb|-}} {{m|nb|sten}}, {{etyl|nn|-}} {{m|nn|stein}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|sten}}, {{etyl|fo|-}} {{m|da|steinur}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|stien}}, {{etyl|nds|-}} {{m|nds|Steen}}. Ultimately from {{der|is|ine-pro|*stāi-||something hard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/steitn/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eitn|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|steins|steinar}}

# [[stone]], [[rock]]
# [[stone]], [[pit]], [[pip]] {{gloss|the seed of certain [[fruit]]}}
# {{lb|is|medicine}} a [[calculus]], a [[stone]]

